## Comprehensive Medical Solutions

Directly from pitchside trauma care to full-family diagnostics. Every treatment protocol combines the precision of elite sports science with compassionate primary care.

### Concussion Assessment & Management
Standardized SCAT5 baseline testing, post-impact cognitive evaluation, vestibular screening, and supervised return-to-sport clearance.

### Diagnosis & Treatment of Sports Injuries
Acute joint sprains, ligament tears, muscle rupture management, tendon rehabilitation, and kinetic chain biomechanics.

### Exercise Prescription Advice
Prescribing movement as medicine. Dose-response exercise plans for hypertension, metabolic health, type 2 diabetes, and longevity.

### Physical Health & Performance Optimisation
Physiological testing, VO2 pacing, heart-rate variability recovery, endurance coaching, and athletic fueling strategies.

### Family Medicine Comprehensive Care
Primary medical care for all ages — from common viral infections and pediatric care to weight loss solutions and chronic disease.

### General Check-ups & Vital Screenings
Blood pressure monitoring, cholesterol lipid profiling, resting ECG, glucose screenings, and proactive cardiovascular assessments.

### Laboratory Testing (Blood Work)
Fast and accurate on-site diagnostics. Monitoring inflammatory markers, hormones, iron, and metabolic panels to optimize wellbeing.

### Family Planning & Contraception
Personalized advice with regards to birth control options, reproductive counseling, and athletic cycle management.

## Movement is Medicine.

“Whether you are returning from a concussion, managing a chronic condition, or optimizing your athletic performance, we provide evidence-based, personalized care.”

### Graduated Return-to-Play Protocol (GRTP)

#### Stage 1: Symptom-Limited Activity
Initial 24–48 hours of physical and mental rest. Daily living activities that do not provoke concussion symptoms (headache, dizziness, photophobia).

